# Valgrind suppressions for the Ghoti.io Image test suite.
#
# Nothing here suppresses an allocation this library makes. Each entry names a
# leak in a system library, reached from test scaffolding, with the measurement
# that established it.

# glibc leaks the locale name when a locale is loaded from a LOCPATH directory
# rather than the system archive. freelocale() releases the locale object and
# not the argz vector newlocale() built for its name.
#
# Established with a five-line program containing no library code at all:
# newlocale(LC_NUMERIC_MASK, "de_DE.UTF-8", 0) followed by freelocale(). With
# the locale resolved from the system archive it is clean - 37 allocs, 37
# frees. With LOCPATH pointing at a localedef-generated directory it leaks 119
# bytes from one block, in that same two-call program.
#
# That second path is the one tests/unit/test_icc_synthesis.cpp takes here,
# because Debian on this machine installs no locale that writes a decimal
# comma, so CommaLocale falls through to generating one with localedef. A
# machine whose archive holds de_DE would never reach it, which is why this
# appeared as a leak on one host and not as a defect in the code.
#
# Scoped to newlocale so it cannot hide an allocation of ours: the frame below
# it is glibc's and the frame above it is whichever test asked for a locale.
{
   glibc-newlocale-keeps-the-locale-name-from-LOCPATH
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect,possible
   ...
   fun:newlocale
   ...
}
